                                "example_id": "d817ec8e-6f40-41a6-a30b-836325c7874f",
                                "sense_id": "956da882-4248-3636-a81e-79a7adebaaa5",
                                "text": "All which my daies I haue not lewdly spent,\nNor spilt the blossome of my tender yeares\nIn ydlesse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "982dc0ee-cd4c-46ee-9569-92bc93863fe2",
                                "sense_id": "956da882-4248-3636-a81e-79a7adebaaa5",
                                "text": "A maiden was seated apart from her companion, the very flowers scattered neglected by her side; but it was obvious that idlesse—that first sweet symptom of love—was pleasanter than her graceful task; for the colour was rich upon her cheek, and the smile parted her scarce conscious lips."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac9c9e7f-1e69-449f-98c1-6655916d9660",
                                "sense_id": "956da882-4248-3636-a81e-79a7adebaaa5",
                                "text": "Next a lover, with a dream\n’Neath his waking eyelids hidden;\nAnd a frequent sigh unbidden'\nAnd an idlesse all the day\nBeside a wandering stream;"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
